* TOOL_CATALOG
* The programs of the account on one screen: what each is, whether and when it was compiled, whether its source has changed since, where it is catalogued, and the verbs that compile
* it, catalogue it and take it out of the catalogue (S.75, plan .claude/plan-fullscreen-toolkit.md sections 2.7, 8 and 12, DV6).  A USER app: any account, the session's own account.
* Copyright (c) 2026, SD Core for Linux.  This program is free software; you can redistribute
* it and/or modify it under the terms of the GNU General Public License, version 3 or later.
*
* START-HISTORY:
* 28 Oct 26 dm  S.88 L2: the two boxes are panes of the layout service ($tk_layout): at 140 by 43 exactly the boxes the page has always drawn, in a bigger window the list shows more programs
*               and the description more lines, both wider; text longer than its box is wrapped when the box is wider than it was.
* 28 Oct 26 dm  S.87: CLOSESEQ and EQU are gone as statements: this program says CLOSE and EQUATE.
* 27 Oct 26 dm  S.87 batch 8: OPTION CATALOGUE.LOCAL is gone, so the page no longer tells of it (the footer note and two refusals).
* 25 Oct 26 dm  New.
* 1 Nov 26 dm  S.97 stage 2: the AI line ($tk_aipage), as tool.voc has it: F6 or AI > Ask the AI; filter and refresh are offered to the model, and a proposal is carried out by
*              the page's own key.  An account without the AI sees the page as it was.
* 1 Nov 26 dm  S.97 stage 4 (the owner's editing actions): B (compile) is offered too, marked 'edit' (Enter alone rejects the proposal); the AI's argument with an accepted filter is the
*              DEFAULT of the filter's text.
* 8 Nov 26 dm  S.176: F6 / Shift-F6 are the box keys of every page ($tk_aipage 'ring'): from the list to the AI line and back; AI > Ask the AI is a menu entry of its own.
* 8 Nov 26 dm  S.179: Ctrl-T the theme (View > Theme) and Ctrl-K the keys of the page (Help > Keys), through $tk_std as on every page.
* 9 Nov 26 dm  S.186: View > Mouse and Ctrl-O (the log of the commands run), the same on every page (act:std.mouse, ctrl-o, $tk_std); a name the page will not give to a command now says why
*              ($tk_badch for the character; why.bad for a first character or a keyword).
* END-HISTORY
*
* START-DESCRIPTION:
*
*   TOOL.CATALOG      (in every account's VOC)
*
*   A full-screen page, in the toolkit's frame (140 columns by 43 lines at least), for the programs of the account the session is in: the records of its program files.  A program file is a
*   VOC entry for a directory file named bp, or ending in .bp, or with a file of the same name and .out beside it (where BASIC puts the compiled programs).  For each record: what it is
*   (program, subroutine, function, class module - read from the compiled program's header - or an include or screen record, which is not compiled by itself), when it was compiled, the size of
*   the compiled program, whether it is current or STALE (the source's file is newer than the compiled program's), and where it is catalogued under its own name: private (a record of the
*   account's cat file, or of the file $PRIVATE.CATALOGUE names), local (a VOC entry V / CS whose pointer leads to its compiled program) or global (an entry of that name in SDSYS's gcat, which
*   this page only reports).  A private copy made by an earlier compile than the compiled program is marked older.  Entries in the private or local catalogue that no program record of the account
*   accounts for are listed too, under the file name (private) or (local), so that they can be taken out.
*
*   WHAT IT CAN DO.  B compiles the program under the cursor (BASIC), C catalogues it privately and L locally (CATALOG), X takes a local entry out AND deletes the compiled program it points at
*   (DECATALOG), D takes a private or a local entry out (DELETE.CATALOG).  Every one of them is the verb the person could type, run through $tk_run after a box that shows the exact command and what
*   it does; X and D, and a catalog that would also take an entry of the same name out of another catalogue, ask for the name, typed.  BASIC and CATALOG are given NO.QUERY: a question they would
*   ask (a replacement, a duplicate in another catalogue) is asked by a prompt the page cannot show, and the box says what NO.QUERY does for that command.  The compiler's own lines (errors and
*   warnings) are shown in a report box.  GLOBAL cataloguing is the administrator's own command and is not offered.  The page changes nothing itself: the verbs' own checks are the wall.  All four
*   need the bp-edit gate (message 12413 from the verb); the page SHOWS the gate, asked of the kernel, and never tries an operation to learn it.
*
*   STALE needs the modification times of two files.  OSPATH() is the only reader of them and it is not gated for a $internal program, so each path is asked of the account's OS gate first
*   (kernel K$PATH.OK: always yes inside the account's own directory) and a path the gate refuses is not read; the state is then shown as ? with the reason.
*
*   Keys: Up and Down, PgUp and PgDn, Home and End move; B, C, L, X, D as above; F11 or / filters the names (a part of a program or file name; empty shows all); Esc clears the filter; F5 reads
*   everything again; F1 or ? or a click on [?] explains the page; Ctrl-Q leaves.  A name with a character the page does not give to a command (a capital, a dollar, a leading dot or dash) is
*   listed and described, and the verbs for it are typed at the prompt.
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
*
* START-CODE

$internal
program $tool_catalog
$catalog $tool_catalog

$include keys.h
$include int$keys.h
$include err.h
$include sl.h
$include tk.h
$include header.h

   prompt ''

   allow = 'basic catalog decatalog delete.catalog'                 ;* the commands this page may run, through $tk_run, after a box
   kwords = ' local global pcode no.query no.catalog noxref no.xref xref relative all changed debugging listing '    ;* words the verbs read as options: never given as a name

   call $tk_open('tool.catalog', '', ctx, err)
   if err # '' then
      display err
      stop
   end

   keys = ''
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'f1', 'help', 'help', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'b', 'compile', 'compile', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'c', 'catalog', 'catalog', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'l', 'local', 'local', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'x', 'decatalog', 'decatalog', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'd', 'remove', 'remove', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, '/', 'filter', 'filter', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'f5', 'refresh', 'refresh', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'ctrl-q', 'quit', 'quit', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'esc', 'menu', 'menu', '', 1)                ;* S.88 U7: Esc takes the name filter off first, else opens the menu bar
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'quit', '&File', '&Quit', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'compile', '&Programs', '&Build (compile)', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'catalog', '&Programs', '&Catalog', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'local', '&Programs', 'Catalog &locally', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'decatalog', '&Programs', 'Decatalog: delete the entry and its object file (&X)', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'remove', '&Programs', '&Delete the catalog entry', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'filter', '&View', '&Filter by name', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'refresh', '&View', '&Refresh', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'help', '&Help', '&Help on this page', '', '')
   call $tk_std('keys', ctx, keys, '', '')                ;* S.179: Ctrl-T theme, Ctrl-K keys and their View and Help entries, as on every page
   * S.97 stage 2: the AI line.  The page offers the AI only the actions that change what is shown (the owner: opt-in, off by default); a proposal is carried out by the page's own
   * key.  Where the AI is not usable for the account nothing here adds a key, a row or a line, and the page is what it always was.
   call $tk_keys('ai', keys, 'filter', '', '', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('ai', keys, 'refresh', '', '', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('ai', keys, 'compile', 'edit', '', '', '')            ;* S.97 stage 4 (the owner's editing actions): compile the program under the cursor, through the page's own Run box
   call $tk_aipage('init', ctx, keys, '', '', aout)

   VIS = 16                                                     ;* program rows on the screen (the list pane's height less 6: set by get.rects)
   rtw = TK.MINW - 2 * TK.XBODY - 4                             ;* the text width of a pane in the reference layout (140 by 43): 134
   perr = ''
   gosub declare.layout
   MAXREC = 2000                                                ;* records read from one program file
   hl = fmt('File', '14L') : ' ' : fmt('Program', '30L') : fmt('Kind', '12L') : fmt('Compiled', '18L') : ' ' : fmt('Object', '8R') : '  ' : fmt('State', '8L') : 'Cataloged'

   rtype = '' ; rfile = '' ; rname = '' ; rlow = '' ; rcls = '' ; rloc = '' ; rpath = '' ; rmeta = '' ; rmc = '' ; nr = 0    ;* every row: type p (a program record) or c (a catalogue entry alone)
   pfn = '' ; pfo = '' ; pfd = '' ; pfq = '' ; pfs = '' ; pfobj = '' ; pfb = '' ; pfc = '' ; npf = 0                       ;* the program files and what is in them
   privn = '' ; privl = '' ; globn = '' ; globl = '' ; locid = '' ; locpath = ''                                          ;* the catalogues, by name
   nprog = 0 ; ncomp = 0 ; npriv = 0 ; nlocal = 0
   pcok = 0 ; gcok = 0 ; pcname = 'cat' ; capnote = ''
   shown = '' ; ns = 0
   filt = ''
   ci = 1 ; ta = 0
   gen = 0
   done = 0
   msg = ''
   meta = '' ; mk = 0 ; lines = '' ; rowtxt = '' ; ctxt = '' ; cmode = '' ; typed.name = ''
   okp = 0 ; pfile = '' ; pname = '' ; want = '' ; sent = '' ; out = '' ; stat = 0 ; rerr = '' ; said = '' ; res = '' ; cmsg = '' ; hm = ''

   gosub open.cats
   gosub read.all
   gosub draw.all
   if capnote # '' then msg = capnote

   loop
      call $tk_menubar('draw', ctx, keys, 'Programs', '', '', mr)           ;* the bar first: it writes row 0 whole, and the frame then writes the app name at its right end
      call $tk_frame(ctx, keys, 'Programs', msg)
      call $sl_curat(0, ctx<TK.C.YSTAT>)
      nm = ''
      screen key returning nm
      mr = ''
      ao = ''
      if nm # '' then call $tk_aipage('key', ctx, keys, 'Programs', nm, ao)          ;* S.97 stage 2: while the AI line has the focus it takes the keys, before the bar sees them
      ai.arg = ''                                                                    ;* S.97 stage 4: the argument of an accepted proposal, the DEFAULT of this page's own prompt for that key
      if ao<1> = 'replay' then nm = ao<2>                                            ;* an action the AI proposed and the person accepted: this page's own key for it
      if ao<1> = 'replay' then ai.arg = ao<5>
      if ao<1> # '' then msg = ao<4>
      busy = (if filt # '' then 1 else 0)
      if nm # '' and ao<1> = '' then call $tk_menubar('key', ctx, keys, 'Programs', nm, busy, mr)       ;* the Esc rule: a name filter is taken off before the bar opens
      if mr<1> # '' then nm = mr<4>
      begin case
         case ao<1> = 'taken'
            if ao<3> then
               gen += 1                                                               ;* the preview, the wait and the answer covered the page: all of it is drawn again
               ctx<TK.C.GEN> = gen
               gosub draw.all
            end
         case nm = ''
            if status() = ER$EOF then exit
         case nm = 'guardquit'
            exit
         case nm = 'resize'
            call $tk_layout('refresh', ctx, '', chg)
            gosub get.rects
            if ta > ns - VIS then ta = ns - VIS
            if ta < 0 then ta = 0
            gen += 1
            ctx<TK.C.GEN> = gen
            gosub draw.all
         case nm = 'mouse'
            gosub on.mouse
         case 1
            gosub on.key
      end case
      if done then exit
   repeat

   call $tk_close(ctx)
   gosub close.cats
   stop

* ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- what the system says

* The private and the global catalogue, opened once.  The private one is the account's cat file, or the directory $PRIVATE.CATALOGUE names, the way the verbs find it; a directory named
* there is opened only if the account's OS gate says it may (a VOC record is the account's own data, and this program is $internal).  Reading is all this page does with either of them.
open.cats:
   pcok = 0
   gcok = 0
   pcname = 'cat'
   prec = ''
   open 'VOC' to vocf then
      read prec from vocf, '$private.catalogue' else
         read prec from vocf, '$private.catalog' else prec = ''
      end
      close vocf
   end
   if upcase(prec[1, 1]) = 'X' and prec<2> # '' then pcname = prec<2>
   pcsafe = 1
   if pcname # 'cat' then
      if not(kernel(K$PATH.OK, ospath(pcname, OS$FULLPATH))) then pcsafe = 0
   end
   if pcsafe then
      openpath pcname to pcf then
         mark.mapping pcf, off
         pcok = 1
      end
   end
   openpath @sdsys : @ds : 'gcat' to gcf then
      mark.mapping gcf, off
      gcok = 1
   end
   return

close.cats:
   if pcok then close pcf
   if gcok then close gcf
   pcok = 0
   gcok = 0
   return

* Everything the lists need: the program files and their record names, the catalogue entries, the rows; the cursor goes back to the row it was on
read.all:
   keep.t = '' ; keep.f = '' ; keep.n = ''
   if ns > 0 and ci >= 1 and ci <= ns then
      kr = shown<ci>
      keep.t = rtype<kr> ; keep.f = rfile<kr> ; keep.n = rname<kr>
   end
   rtype = '' ; rfile = '' ; rname = '' ; rlow = '' ; rcls = '' ; rloc = '' ; rpath = '' ; rmeta = '' ; rmc = '' ; nr = 0
   capnote = ''
   gosub list.pfiles
   gosub list.cats
   gosub build.rows
   gosub apply.filter
   ci = 1
   if keep.n # '' then
      for ki = 1 to ns
         kr = shown<ki>
         if rtype<kr> = keep.t and rfile<kr> = keep.f and rname<kr> = keep.n then
            ci = ki
            exit
         end
      next ki
   end
   if ci > ns then ci = ns
   if ci < 1 then ci = 1
   return

* The VOC: the program files (what is in them is read here, once), and the local catalogue entries (V / CS records)
list.pfiles:
   pfn = '' ; pfo = '' ; pfd = '' ; pfq = '' ; pfs = '' ; pfobj = '' ; npf = 0
   locid = '' ; locpath = ''
   nloc = 0
   open 'VOC' to vocf else return
   sselect vocf to 9
   readlist ids from 9 else ids = ''
   n = dcount(ids, @fm)
   if ids = '' then n = 0
   for i = 1 to n
      vn = ids<i>
      read vr from vocf, vn then
         t1 = upcase(vr<1>)
         if t1 = 'V' and upcase(vr<2>) = 'CS' then
            nloc += 1
            locid<nloc> = vn
            locpath<nloc> = (if vr<3> = '' then '-' else vr<3>)
         end
         if t1 = 'F' or t1[1, 5] = 'FILE ' then gosub test.pfile
      end
   next i
   close vocf
   return

* In: vn, the name of a VOC file entry, and vocf.  Adds it to the program files when it is one: a directory file named bp, or ending .bp, or with a .out file beside it
test.pfile:
   tl = downcase(vn)
   if len(tl) > 4 and tl[len(tl) - 3, 4] = '.out' then return
   isp = (tl = 'bp')
   if len(tl) > 3 and tl[len(tl) - 2, 3] = '.bp' then isp = 1
   if not(isp) then
      read orr from vocf, vn : '.out' then
         if upcase(orr[1, 1]) = 'F' then isp = 1
      end
   end
   if not(isp) then return
   open vn to fv else return
   if fileinfo(fv, FL$TYPE) # FL$TYPE.DIR then
      close fv
      return
   end
   sdir = fileinfo(fv, FL$PATH)
   sselect fv to 8
   readlist snames from 8 else snames = ''
   close fv
   scnt = dcount(snames, @fm)
   if snames = '' then scnt = 0
   if scnt > MAXREC then
      capnote = vn : ' has ' : scnt : ' records: the first ' : MAXREC : ' are listed'
      snames = field(snames, @fm, 1, MAXREC)
   end
   odir = '-'
   onames = ''
   open vn : '.out' to ov then
      if fileinfo(ov, FL$TYPE) = FL$TYPE.DIR then
         odir = fileinfo(ov, FL$PATH)
         sselect ov to 8
         readlist onames from 8 else onames = ''
      end
      close ov
   end
   npf += 1
   pfn<npf> = vn
   pfo<npf> = vn : '.out'
   pfd<npf> = sdir
   pfq<npf> = odir
   pfs<npf> = convert(@fm, @vm, snames)
   pfobj<npf> = convert(@fm, @vm, onames)
   return

* The names in the private and the global catalogue
list.cats:
   privn = '' ; globn = ''
   if pcok then
      select pcf to 7
      readlist privn from 7 else privn = ''
   end
   if gcok then
      select gcf to 7
      readlist globn from 7 else globn = ''
   end
   privl = downcase(privn)
   globl = downcase(globn)
   npriv = dcount(privn, @fm)
   if privn = '' then npriv = 0
   return

* The rows: the program records of each file in name order, then the private and local entries no program record accounts for
build.rows:
   nr = 0
   nprog = 0
   ncomp = 0
   for bj = 1 to npf
      pfb<bj> = nr
      pcnt = dcount(pfs<bj>, @vm)
      if pfs<bj> = '' then pcnt = 0
      pfc<bj> = pcnt
      ostr = downcase(@vm : pfobj<bj> : @vm)
      for bk = 1 to pcnt
         bn = pfs<bj, bk>
         nr += 1
         rtype<nr> = 'p'
         rfile<nr> = pfn<bj>
         rname<nr> = bn
         rlow<nr> = downcase(bn)
         rn = bn
         gosub rec.class
         rcls<nr> = rclass
         if rclass = '' then
            nprog += 1
            if index(ostr, @vm : downcase(bn) : @vm, 1) > 0 then ncomp += 1
         end
      next bk
   next bj
   for bi = 1 to npriv
      bn = privn<bi>
      bp2 = 0
      locate downcase(bn) in rlow<1> setting bp2 else bp2 = 0
      if bp2 = 0 then
         nr += 1
         rtype<nr> = 'c'
         rfile<nr> = '(private)'
         rname<nr> = bn
         rlow<nr> = downcase(bn)
         rcls<nr> = ''
      end
   next bi
   for bi = 1 to nloc
      lp = locpath<bi>
      if lp[1, 1] # @ds then lp = @path : @ds : lp
      lpl = downcase(lp)
      hit = 0
      for bj = 1 to npf
         if pfq<bj> # '-' then
            pre = downcase(pfq<bj>) : @ds
            if lpl[1, len(pre)] = pre then
               onm = lpl[len(pre) + 1, 999]
               for bk = 1 to pfc<bj>
                  if downcase(pfs<bj, bk>) = onm then
                     rr = pfb<bj> + bk
                     rloc<rr, -1> = locid<bi>
                     hit = 1
                     exit
                  end
               next bk
            end
         end
         if hit then exit
      next bj
      if not(hit) then
         nr += 1
         rtype<nr> = 'c'
         rfile<nr> = '(local)'
         rname<nr> = locid<bi>
         rlow<nr> = downcase(locid<bi>)
         rcls<nr> = ''
         rloc<nr> = locid<bi>
         rpath<nr> = lp
      end
   next bi
   nlocal = nloc
   return

* In: rn.  Out: rclass, '' for a record the compiler takes as a program, else include, screen or options (the records BASIC skips when it compiles a whole file)
rec.class:
   rclass = ''
   cl = downcase(rn)
   if cl = '$basic.options' then
      rclass = 'options'
   end else
      cparts = dcount(cl, '.')
      if cparts > 1 then
         csuf = field(cl, '.', cparts)
         if csuf = 'h' then rclass = 'include'
         if csuf = 'scr' then rclass = 'screen'
      end
   end
   return

* The rows that hold the filter's text in their program or file name (any case), in the order they were built
apply.filter:
   shown = ''
   ns = 0
   for fi = 1 to nr
      if filt = '' or index(upcase(rname<fi> : ' ' : rfile<fi>), upcase(filt), 1) > 0 then
         ns += 1
         shown<ns> = fi
      end
   next fi
   return

* ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- what is known about one row

* In: mk, the row.  Out: meta, a field of values (below); read once per row until the next F5 or action.
*   1 kind  2 compile time  3 object bytes  4 state (current, stale, ?, -)  5 private (same older newer there or null)  6 global (1 or 0)  7 source bytes  8 source modified, epoch
*   9 object modified, epoch  10 flags  11 source path  12 object path  13 private copy's compile time  14 class (include screen options or null)  15 arguments
*   16 compile time as text  17 private copy's compile time as text  18 source modified as text  19 why the state is ?
ensure.meta:
   if rmc<mk> = 1 then
      meta = rmeta<mk>
      return
   end
   mkind = '' ; mct = '' ; mosz = '' ; mstate = '-' ; mpriv = '' ; mglob = 0 ; msize = '' ; msm = '' ; mom = '' ; mflags = '' ; msp = '' ; mop = '' ; mpct = ''
   mcls = rcls<mk> ; margs = '' ; mctxt = '' ; mpstamp = '' ; msstamp = '' ; mreason = ''
   rn = rname<mk>
   if rtype<mk> = 'p' then
      gosub meta.program
   end else
      gosub meta.entry
   end
   meta = mkind : @vm : mct : @vm : mosz : @vm : mstate : @vm : mpriv : @vm : mglob : @vm : msize : @vm : msm : @vm : mom : @vm : mflags : @vm : msp : @vm : mop : @vm : mpct : @vm : mcls : @vm : margs : @vm : mctxt : @vm : mpstamp : @vm : msstamp : @vm : mreason
   rmeta<mk> = meta
   rmc<mk> = 1
   return

meta.program:
   bj = 0
   for q1 = 1 to npf
      if pfn<q1> = rfile<mk> then bj = q1
   next q1
   msp = pfd<bj> : @ds : rn
   mop = ''
   if pfq<bj> # '-' then mop = pfq<bj> : @ds : rn
   obj = ''
   if mop # '' then
      open pfo<bj> to ov then
         mark.mapping ov, off
         read obj from ov, rn else obj = ''
         close ov
      end
   end
   if obj # '' then
      pin = obj
      gosub parse.obj
      mosz = len(obj)
      mkind = pkind ; mct = pct ; mflags = pflags ; margs = pargs
      stin = mct
      gosub stamp
      mctxt = sstr
      mstate = '?'
      gosub src.times
   end
   if mcls # '' then mkind = mcls
   if pcok then
      locate downcase(rn) in privl<1> setting pp else pp = 0
      if pp > 0 then
         pobj = ''
         read pobj from pcf, rn else pobj = ''
         mpriv = 'there'
         if pobj # '' then
            pin = pobj
            gosub parse.obj
            mpct = pct
            stin = pct
            gosub stamp
            mpstamp = sstr
            if pok and mct # '' then
               mpriv = (if pct = mct then 'same' else (if pct + 0 < mct + 0 then 'older' else 'newer'))
            end
         end
      end
   end
   if gcok then
      locate downcase(rn) in globl<1> setting gp else gp = 0
      if gp > 0 then mglob = 1
   end
   return

* A catalogue entry no program record accounts for: the private copy, or the object a local entry points at
meta.entry:
   if rfile<mk> = '(private)' then
      mpriv = 'there'
      pobj = ''
      read pobj from pcf, rn else pobj = ''
      if pobj # '' then
         pin = pobj
         gosub parse.obj
         mkind = pkind ; mct = pct ; mflags = pflags ; margs = pargs
         mosz = len(pobj)
         stin = mct
         gosub stamp
         mctxt = sstr
      end
   end else
      mop = rpath<mk>
      if mop = '' or not(kernel(K$PATH.OK, mop)) then
         mreason = 'the pointer leads outside the account, which the account may not read'
      end else
         openseq mop readonly to sf then
            blk = ''
            readblk blk from sf, 256 else blk = ''
            close sf
            pin = blk
            gosub parse.obj
            mkind = pkind ; mct = pct ; mflags = pflags ; margs = pargs
            stin = mct
            gosub stamp
            mctxt = sstr
            oi = ospath(mop, OS$INFO)
            mosz = oi<6>
         end else
            if not(unassigned(sf)) then close sf       ;* 26 Oct 26 - an OPENSEQ that took ELSE keeps the name locked until the variable is closed (see home_entry)
            mreason = 'the object it points at is not there'
         end
      end
   end
   return

* In: pin, the bytes of an object record.  Out: pok, pkind, pct (compile time), pflags (text), pargs
parse.obj:
   pok = 0 ; pkind = '' ; pct = '' ; pflags = '' ; pargs = ''
   if pin[1, 1] = char(100) or pin[1, 1] = char(101) then
      pok = 1
      pct = oconv(pin[HDR.COMPILE.TIME, 4], 'IL')
      hf = seq(pin[HDR.FLAGS, 1]) + 256 * seq(pin[HDR.FLAGS + 1, 1])
      pargs = seq(pin[HDR.ARGS, 1]) + 256 * seq(pin[HDR.ARGS + 1, 1])
      begin case
         case bitand(hf, HDR.IS.CLASS)
            pkind = 'class'
         case bitand(hf, HDR.IS.FUNCTION)
            pkind = 'function'
            pargs = max(pargs - 1, 0)                           ;* the object counts a function's hidden return variable
         case pargs > 0
            pkind = 'subroutine'
         case 1
            pkind = 'program'
      end case
      fl2 = ''
      if bitand(hf, HDR.INTERNAL) then fl2<-1> = 'internal'
      if bitand(hf, HDR.DEBUG) then fl2<-1> = 'debug'
      if bitand(hf, HDR.RECURSIVE) then fl2<-1> = 'recursive'
      pflags = change(fl2, @fm, ', ')
   end
   return

* In: stin, a time as the object header holds it (seconds).  Out: sstr, the date and time as text, or null
stamp:
   sstr = ''
   if stin # '' then sstr = oconv(int(stin / 86400), 'D2DMYL[,A3]') : ' ' : oconv(rem(stin, 86400), 'MTS')
   return

* In: rn, msp, mop.  Sets msize, msm, mom, msstamp and mstate (current or stale) when both files can be read; else mstate stays ? and mreason says why.  The modification times
* come from OSPATH(), which does not ask the OS gate for a $internal program, so each path is asked of the gate here first.
src.times:
   fn = rn
   gosub check.name
   if not(okname) then
      mreason = 'the name has a character the page does not give to a command'
      return
   end
   if not(kernel(K$PATH.OK, msp)) or not(kernel(K$PATH.OK, mop)) then
      mreason = 'a path is outside the account and its OS gate is off'
      return
   end
   si = ospath(msp, OS$INFO)
   oi = ospath(mop, OS$INFO)
   if si = '' or oi = '' then
      mreason = 'a file is not there to be read'
      return
   end
   msize = si<6>
   msm = si<35>
   mom = oi<35>
   msstamp = oconv(si<16>, 'D2DMYL[,A3]') : ' ' : oconv(si<15>, 'MTS')
   if msm = '' or mom = '' then
      mreason = 'the system gave no time'
      return
   end
   mstate = (if msm + 0 > mom + 0 then 'stale' else 'current')
   return

* ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- drawing

* The layout (S.88 L2).  The two boxes are the panes of the layout service, declared in the sizes of the reference layout (140 by 43, the body 138 by 39): the list stretches (a bigger
* window shows more programs), the description takes what the layout gives it by its own weight of columns and rows.
* Out: lx ly lw lh (the list), dx dy dw dh (the description), tw (the text width of both), VIS (the program rows).
declare.layout:
   d = ''
   d<1> = 'list' : @vm : 1 : @vm : 1 : @vm : 22 : @vm : 138 : @vm : '' : @vm : 'stretch' : @vm : 1 : @vm : 'stretch' : @vm : 1
   d<2> = 'detail' : @vm : 2 : @vm : 1 : @vm : 17 : @vm : 138 : @vm : '' : @vm : '' : @vm : '' : @vm : 'stretch' : @vm : 1
   call $tk_layout('declare', ctx, d, perr)
   gosub get.rects
   return

get.rects:
   call $tk_layout('pane', ctx, 'list', rc)
   lx = rc<1, 1> ; ly = rc<1, 2> ; lw = rc<1, 3> ; lh = rc<1, 4>
   call $tk_layout('pane', ctx, 'detail', rc)
   dx = rc<1, 1> ; dy = rc<1, 2> ; dw = rc<1, 3> ; dh = rc<1, 4>
   tw = lw - 4
   VIS = lh - 6                                                 ;* the header row, the program rows, the two summary lines, a blank row and the border: 16 rows of 22
   return

* In: lines.  Out: dlines, what the description shows.  At the reference width a line longer than the box is cut, as it has always been; in a wider box it is wrapped
fit.lines:
   dlines = lines
   if tw > rtw then
      dlines = ''
      nd = 0
      for q = 1 to dcount(lines, @fm)
         nd += 1
         dlines<nd> = ''
         if lines<q> # '' then
            call $tk_wrap(lines<q>, tw, wpieces)
            for pj = 1 to dcount(wpieces, @fm)
               dlines<nd> = wpieces<pj>
               nd += 1
            next pj
            nd -= 1
         end
      next q
   end
   return

draw.all:
   cw2 = ctx<TK.C.W>
   chh = ctx<TK.C.H> - 5
   screen clear at 0,1 size cw2,chh
   ttl = 'Programs in ' : @who
   screen box at lx,ly size lw,lh title ttl
   screen box at dx,dy size dw,dh title 'The program under the cursor'
   gosub draw.list
   gosub draw.detail
   return

draw.list:
   screen text hl at lx + 2,ly + 1 attr 'header' width tw
   if ci <= ta then ta = ci - 1
   if ci > ta + VIS then ta = ci - VIS
   if ta < 0 then ta = 0
   for r = 1 to VIS
      kk = ta + r
      s = ''
      if kk <= ns then
         mk = shown<kk>
         gosub ensure.meta
         gosub row.text
         s = rowtxt
      end
      screen text s at lx + 2,ly + 1 + r attr (if kk = ci and kk <= ns then 'highlight' else 'normal') width tw
   next r
   gosub draw.foot
   call $tk_help('mark', lx + lw - 5, ly + 1, 0, 0)
   return

* In: mk, meta.  Out: rowtxt
row.text:
   rk = meta<1, 1>
   if rk = '' then rk = '-'
   rs = meta<1, 4>
   if rtype<mk> = 'c' then rs = ''                               ;* an entry alone has no source to compare with
   rowtxt = fmt(rfile<mk>, '14L') : ' ' : fmt(rname<mk>, '30L') : fmt(rk, '12L') : fmt(meta<1, 16>, '18L') : ' ' : fmt(meta<1, 3>, '8R') : '  ' : fmt(rs, '8L')
   gosub cat.text
   rowtxt := ctxt
   return

* In: mk, meta.  Out: ctxt, where the program is catalogued, in a few words
cat.text:
   ctxt = ''
   pv = meta<1, 5>
   if pv # '' then
      ctxt<-1> = 'private' : (if pv = 'older' then ' (older)' else (if pv = 'newer' then ' (newer)' else ''))
   end
   lv = rloc<mk, 1>
   if lv # '' then
      ctxt<-1> = 'local' : (if downcase(lv) # downcase(rname<mk>) then ' as ' : lv else '')
   end
   if meta<1, 6> = 1 then ctxt<-1> = 'global'
   ctxt = change(ctxt, @fm, ', ')
   return

* The summary under the list, and the gate this session holds (asked of the kernel, never tried)
* Out: gon = 1 when this session may compile and catalogue; gadm = 1 when it is the administrator.  The verbs refuse a session that is neither the administrator nor holding bp-edit (they test
* 'not K$ADMINISTRATOR and not K$BP.EDIT'), so the raw bp-edit bit alone would tell the administrator the gate is off
gate.state:
   gadm = kernel(K$ADMINISTRATOR, -1)
   gon = (gadm or kernel(K$BP.EDIT, -1))
   return

draw.foot:
   gosub gate.state
   s = 'Your gate:  bp-edit ' : (if gon then (if gadm then 'on (administrator)' else 'on') else 'off')
   s := '   ' : nprog : (if nprog = 1 then ' program' else ' programs') : ' in ' : npf : (if npf = 1 then ' file' else ' files') : ', ' : ncomp : ' compiled; ' : npriv : ' private and ' : nlocal : ' local catalog '
   s := (if npriv + nlocal = 1 then 'entry' else 'entries')
   if filt # '' then s := ', ' : ns : ' shown with "' : filt : '"'
   screen text fmt(s, tw : 'L') at lx + 2,ly + lh - 4 attr 'bold' width tw
   note = "basic, catalog, decatalog and delete.catalog need bp-edit; what refuses is the verb.  Global cataloging is the administrator's own command and is not offered here."
   wpieces = note
   if tw > rtw then call $tk_wrap(note, tw, wpieces)
   screen text fmt(wpieces<1>, tw : 'L') at lx + 2,ly + lh - 3 width tw
   if wpieces<2> # '' then screen text fmt(wpieces<2>, tw : 'L') at lx + 2,ly + lh - 2 width tw
   return

* The row under the cursor in plain words
draw.detail:
   lines = ''
   if ns >= 1 and ci >= 1 and ci <= ns then
      mk = shown<ci>
      gosub ensure.meta
      gosub describe
   end else
      if nr = 0 then
         lines<-1> = 'This account has no program file yet: a file named bp, or ending in .bp, or with a .out file beside it.'
         lines<-1> = 'create.file bp directory makes one (the files page, tool.files, N, does it too); put a program in it with sed or the ide, and B compiles it.'
      end else
         lines<-1> = 'No program or file name holds "' : filt : '".  Esc shows all of them.'
      end
   end
   gosub fit.lines
   for r = 1 to dh - 2
      screen text fmt(dlines<r>[1, tw], tw : 'L') at dx + 2,dy + r width tw
   next r
   return

* In: mk, meta.  Out: lines, the description in sentences
describe:
   rn = rname<mk>
   mkind = meta<1, 1>
   if rtype<mk> = 'c' then
      gosub describe.entry
      return
   end
   begin case
      case meta<1, 14> = 'include'
         what = 'an include record: other programs take it in with $include; it is not compiled by itself.'
      case meta<1, 14> = 'screen'
         what = 'a screen definition record; it is not compiled by itself.'
      case meta<1, 14> = 'options'
         what = 'the compiler options of the file; BASIC skips it when it compiles a whole file.'
      case mkind = 'program'
         what = 'a program.'
      case mkind = 'subroutine'
         what = 'a subroutine with ' : meta<1, 15> : (if meta<1, 15> = 1 then ' argument.' else ' arguments.')
      case mkind = 'function'
         what = 'a function with ' : meta<1, 15> : (if meta<1, 15> = 1 then ' argument.' else ' arguments.')
      case mkind = 'class'
         what = 'a class module.'
      case 1
         what = 'not compiled yet.  B compiles it.'
   end case
   lines<-1> = rfile<mk> : ' / ' : rn : '  -  ' : what
   s = 'Source:  ' : meta<1, 11>
   if meta<1, 7> # '' then s := '  (' : meta<1, 7> : ' bytes, changed ' : meta<1, 18> : ')'
   lines<-1> = s
   if meta<1, 3> # '' then
      s = 'Object:  ' : meta<1, 12> : '  (' : meta<1, 3> : ' bytes, compiled ' : meta<1, 16> : (if meta<1, 10> # '' then '; ' : meta<1, 10> else '') : ')'
      lines<-1> = s
      begin case
         case meta<1, 4> = 'current'
            lines<-1> = 'The compiled program is current: the source has not been changed since it was compiled.'
         case meta<1, 4> = 'stale'
            lines<-1> = 'STALE: the source was changed after the program was compiled.  B compiles it again.'
         case 1
            lines<-1> = 'The page cannot tell whether the source was changed since it was compiled: ' : meta<1, 19> : '.'
      end case
   end else
      if meta<1, 14> = '' then lines<-1> = 'There is no compiled program in ' : rfile<mk> : '.out for it.'
   end
   lines<-1> = ''
   lines<-1> = 'Catalog entries under the call name ' : rn : ' (typing the name runs the program once it is cataloged):'
   pv = meta<1, 5>
   begin case
      case pv = ''
         s = 'none.  C puts it there.'
      case pv = 'same'
         s = 'yes, the same compile as the compiled program.'
      case pv = 'older'
         s = 'yes, but from an earlier compile (' : meta<1, 17> : ').  C catalogs the current one.'
      case pv = 'newer'
         s = 'yes, but from a LATER compile (' : meta<1, 17> : ') than the compiled program in ' : rfile<mk> : '.out.'
      case 1
         s = 'yes (the compiled program it was made from is not here).'
   end case
   lines<-1> = "   private  (your account's cat file):  " : s
   if rloc<mk> = '' then
      lines<-1> = '   local    (a VOC entry):  none.  L puts it there.'
   end else
      lines<-1> = '   local    (a VOC entry):  yes, ' : change(rloc<mk>, @vm, ' ') : ' points at the compiled program.  X takes it out and deletes the compiled program; D takes only the entry out.'
   end
   if meta<1, 6> = 1 then
      lines<-1> = "   global   (SDSYS's gcat):  an entry of that name exists; the page cannot tell whether it is this program.  Only the administrator changes it."
   end else
      lines<-1> = "   global   (SDSYS's gcat):  none."
   end
   lines<-1> = ''
   lines<-1> = 'To run it before it is cataloged:  run ' : rfile<mk> : ' ' : rn
   return

* In: mk, meta.  Out: lines, for a catalogue entry that no program record accounts for
describe.entry:
   rn = rname<mk>
   if rfile<mk> = '(private)' then
      lines<-1> = rn : "  -  an entry in the private catalog (your account's cat file) that no program record of your program files accounts for."
      lines<-1> = 'Typing ' : rn : ' runs it.  D takes the entry out (delete.catalog ' : rn : ').'
   end else
      lines<-1> = rn : '  -  a local catalog entry (a VOC entry) that points at ' : rpath<mk>
      lines<-1> = 'No program record of your program files accounts for it.  X takes it out and deletes the object it points at (decatalog).'
      lines<-1> = 'D takes only the entry out (delete.catalog ' : rn : ' local).'
   end
   if mkind # '' then
      s = 'It is ' : (if mkind = 'program' then 'a program' else 'a ' : mkind) : ', compiled ' : meta<1, 16> : ', ' : meta<1, 3> : ' bytes.'
      lines<-1> = s
   end else
      if meta<1, 19> # '' then
         lines<-1> = 'The page cannot read the object: ' : meta<1, 19> : '.'
      end else
         lines<-1> = 'The page cannot read what the entry holds.'
      end
   end
   return

* ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- keys and mouse

on.key:
   msg = ''
   if len(nm) = 1 then nm = downcase(nm)                         ;* B and b are one key
   begin case
      case nm = 'esc'
         if filt # '' then
            filt = ''
            gosub apply.filter
            ci = 1 ; ta = 0
            gosub draw.all
         end
      case nm = 'up'
         if ci > 1 then
            ci -= 1
            gosub redraw
         end
      case nm = 'down'
         if ci < ns then
            ci += 1
            gosub redraw
         end
      case nm = 'pgup'
         ci -= VIS
         if ci < 1 then ci = 1
         gosub redraw
      case nm = 'pgdn'
         ci += VIS
         if ci > ns then ci = ns
         gosub redraw
      case nm = 'home'
         ci = 1
         gosub redraw
      case nm = 'end'
         if ns > 0 then ci = ns
         gosub redraw
      case nm = 'b'
         gosub do.basic
      case nm = 'c'
         cmode = ''
         gosub do.cat
      case nm = 'l'
         cmode = 'local'
         gosub do.cat
      case nm = 'x'
         gosub do.decat
      case nm = 'd'
         gosub do.delcat
      case nm = 'f11' or nm = '/'
         gosub do.filter
      case nm = 'f1' or nm = '?'
         call $tk_help('box', 'tool.catalog.page', hm, 0, 0)
         if hm # '' then msg = hm
      case nm = 'ctrl-t'                    ;* S.179: the theme, kept for the person - the same on every page ($tk_std)
         call $tk_std('theme', ctx, keys, '', std.r)
         if std.r<1> then gosub draw.all
         msg = std.r<2>
      case nm = 'act:std.mouse'             ;* S.186: View > Mouse, the same on every page ($tk_std)
         call $tk_std('mouse', ctx, keys, '', std.r)
         msg = std.r<2>
      case nm = 'ctrl-o'                    ;* S.186: the log of the commands this page ran (View > Output; $tk_std)
         call $tk_std('output', ctx, keys, '', std.r)
      case nm = 'ctrl-k'                    ;* S.179: the keys of this page, in a box
         call $tk_std('keylist', ctx, keys, 'Programs', std.r)
      case nm = 'f5'
         gosub read.all
         gosub draw.all
         msg = 'read the programs and the catalogs again'
         if capnote # '' then msg = capnote
      case nm = 'f6' or nm = 'shift-f6' or nm = 'act:ai'
         call $tk_aipage('ring', ctx, keys, 1, nm : @fm : 1, ap)            ;* S.176: F6 / Shift-F6 go round the boxes (one here) and the AI line; AI > Ask the AI goes to the line
         msg = ap<2>
      case nm = 'ctrl-q'
         done = 1
   end case
   return

redraw:
   gosub draw.all
   return

on.mouse:
   screen mouse returning mev else mev = ''
   if mev = '' then return
   mr = ''
   call $tk_menubar('click', ctx, keys, 'Programs', mev, '', mr)                  ;* a click on the bar on row 0
   if mr<1> # '' then
      nm = mr<4>
      if nm # '' then gosub on.key                          ;* a bar left with nothing chosen has no name: the status message stays
      return
   end
   call $tk_aipage('mouse', ctx, keys, 'Programs', mev, ap)                         ;* S.97 stage 2: a click on the AI line gives it the focus
   if ap # '' then
      msg = ap
      return
   end
   call $tk_help('hit', mev, lx + lw - 5, ly + 1, hit.m)
   if hit.m then
      call $tk_help('box', 'tool.catalog.page', hm, 0, 0)
      if hm # '' then msg = hm
      return
   end
   if mev<1> = 'press' and mev<2> = 1 then
      mx = mev<3>
      my = mev<4>
      if mx >= lx + 2 and mx <= lx + lw - 3 and my >= ly + 2 and my <= ly + 1 + VIS then
         if ta + my - (ly + 1) <= ns then
            ci = ta + my - (ly + 1)
            gosub redraw
         end
      end
   end
   return

* ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- the things the page can run

* A name the page may give to a command: letters a-z, digits, dot, dash and underscore only (what $tk_run lets through)
* 9 Nov 26 (S.186): why a catalogue entry's name (bad.w) is not given to a command, in words, for the status line: the character ($tk_badch), else the first
*   character that is not a letter or a digit (the verbs read such a name as a global one), else a keyword's name, else its length
why.bad:
   call $tk_badch(bad.w, bad.ch)
   begin case
      case bad.ch # ''
         bad.ch = 'has ' : bad.ch
      case index('abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789', bad.w[1, 1], 1) = 0
         bad.ch = 'begins with ' : (if bad.w = '' then 'nothing' else bad.w[1, 1])
      case index(kwords, ' ' : downcase(bad.w) : ' ', 1) > 0
         bad.ch = 'is a keyword'
      case 1
         bad.ch = 'has more than 63 characters'
   end case
   return

check.name:
   okname = (len(fn) > 0 and len(fn) <= 63)
   good = 'abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789._-'
   for q = 1 to len(fn)
      if index(good, fn[q, 1], 1) = 0 then okname = @false
   next q
   return

* The program under the cursor as the one B, C and L act on.  In: want, the verb to type instead.  Out: okp (1 when the page may build a command), pfile, pname, mk, meta; msg says why not
pick.program:
   okp = 0
   if ns < 1 then return
   mk = shown<ci>
   gosub ensure.meta
   if rtype<mk> # 'p' then
      msg = 'this is a catalog entry with no program record in your files: X takes a local one out, D a private or a local one'
      return
   end
   if meta<1, 14> # '' then
      msg = 'this record is not compiled by itself (an include, a screen definition or the compiler options): nothing to compile or catalog'
      return
   end
   pfile = rfile<mk>
   pname = rname<mk>
   fn = pfile
   gosub check.name
   ok1 = okname
   fn = pname
   gosub check.name
   if not(ok1 and okname) then
      call $tk_badch(pfile : pname, bad.ch)                        ;* 9 Nov 26 (S.186): say which character
      if bad.ch = '' then bad.ch = 'more than 63 characters'
      msg = 'this name has ' : bad.ch : ', which the page does not give to a command: type ' : want : ' ' : pfile : ' ' : pname : ' at the prompt'
      return
   end
   if index('abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789', pname[1, 1], 1) = 0 or index('abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789', pfile[1, 1], 1) = 0 then
      msg = 'a name that begins with a dot, a dash or an underscore is read by the verbs as a global name: type ' : want : ' ' : pfile : ' ' : pname : ' at the prompt'
      return
   end
   if index(kwords, ' ' : downcase(pname) : ' ', 1) > 0 or index(kwords, ' ' : downcase(pfile) : ' ', 1) > 0 then
      msg = 'the name is a word the verbs read as an option (local, global, no.query ...), so no command can name it: rename the record first'
      return
   end
   okp = 1
   return

* Run sent, the box having been answered Run.  Out: out (the lines the verb printed), stat (its return code), rerr (null when it ran)
run.sent:
   call $tk_run(allow, sent, out, stat, rerr)
   out = change(change(change(out, char(13) : char(10), @fm), char(10), @fm), char(13), '')
   gosub first.line
   return

first.line:
   said = ''
   for oi2 = 1 to dcount(out, @fm)
      if trim(out<oi2>) # '' then
         said = trim(out<oi2>)
         exit
      end
   next oi2
   return

* The lines of the gate warning, when bp-edit is off for the session
gate.line:
   gosub gate.state
   if not(gon) then
      lines<-1> = ''
      lines<-1> = 'Your bp-edit gate is off, so the verb will refuse and nothing will change.  The administrator turns the gate on with modify.account.'
   end
   return

* After a command: read everything again and put the cursor back on the row it was on
after.run:
   gosub read.all
   gosub draw.all
   return

* B: compile the program under the cursor and show the compiler's lines
do.basic:
   want = 'basic'
   gosub pick.program
   if not(okp) then return
   sent = 'basic ' : pfile : ' ' : pname : ' no.query'
   lines = ''
   lines<-1> = 'Compiles ' : pname : ' of the file ' : pfile : ' and writes the result to ' : pfile : ".out.  The compiled program that is there is removed first and is not put back if the compile fails.  The compiler's lines are shown afterwards."
   lines<-1> = 'no.query keeps the compiler from asking a question the page cannot show: a source with a $catalog line is cataloged by its compile, and an entry of the same name in another catalog is then replaced without asking.'
   gosub gate.line
   call $tk_confirm(sent, lines, '', res, cmsg)
   if res # 'run' then
      msg = cmsg
      return
   end
   gosub run.sent
   if rerr # '' then
      msg = rerr
      return
   end
   if stat < 0 then
      msg = (if said # '' then said else sent : ' was refused')
      return
   end
   gosub show.report
   msg = (if stat > 0 then pname : ' compiled with no errors' else pname : ' did not compile: the report has the compiler lines')
   gosub after.run
   return

* The compiler's output in a box.  In: sent, out
show.report:
   call $sl_scr('get', scr)
   wrapw = scr<SL.S.W> - 16
   if wrapw > 100 then wrapw = 100
   if wrapw < 20 then wrapw = 20
   body = ''
   nout = dcount(out, @fm)
   if out = '' then nout = 0
   for ri = 1 to nout
      if dcount(body, @fm) < 24 then
         call $tk_wrap(trimb(out<ri>), wrapw, pieces)
         body<-1> = pieces
      end
   next ri
   if nout > 0 then
      if dcount(body, @fm) >= 24 then body<-1> = '...'
   end
   if body = '' then body = 'the compiler printed nothing'
   screen msgbox body title sent buttons '&Close' default 1 returning b else b = 0
   if b = char(1) then null                                    ;* the answer is not used: Close is the only button
   return

* C and L: catalogue the compiled program under the cursor, privately (cmode null) or locally
do.cat:
   want = 'catalog'
   gosub pick.program
   if not(okp) then return
   if meta<1, 3> = '' then
      msg = pname : ' is not compiled yet: B compiles it, and then it can be cataloged'
      return
   end
   sent = 'catalog ' : pfile : ' ' : pname : (if cmode = 'local' then ' local' else '') : ' no.query'
   * the verbs act by NAME, not by what an entry points at: catalog removes (C) or replaces (L) a local entry called this under no.query whatever program it points at, so the entry of that
   * name is looked for by name, and a name is asked for when it is one that points at another program
   sname = downcase(pname)
   lq = 0
   locate sname in locid<1> setting lq else lq = 0
   lfound = (lq > 0)
   lhere = (lfound and index(@vm : rloc<mk> : @vm, @vm : sname : @vm, 1) > 0)
   others = ''
   if cmode = '' then
      if lfound then others<-1> = 'the local entry ' : sname : (if lhere then '' else ' (it points at another program)')
      if meta<1, 6> = 1 then others<-1> = 'the global entry ' : pname
   end else
      if lfound and not(lhere) then others<-1> = 'the local entry ' : sname : ' (it points at another program and is replaced)'
      if meta<1, 5> # '' then others<-1> = 'the private copy of ' : pname
      if meta<1, 6> = 1 then others<-1> = 'the global entry ' : pname
   end
   lines = ''
   if cmode = '' then
      lines<-1> = 'Copies the compiled program ' : pname : " into the private catalog (your account's cat file).  Typing " : downcase(pname) : ' at the prompt then runs it.'
      if meta<1, 5> # '' then lines<-1> = 'The private copy that is there is replaced.'
   end else
      lines<-1> = 'Makes a local catalog entry: a VOC entry ' : downcase(pname) : ' that points at the compiled program in ' : pfile : '.out.  Typing ' : downcase(pname) : ' runs it, in this account only.'
      if lfound then lines<-1> = 'A local entry of that name is already there; it is replaced' : (if lhere then '.' else ', although it points at another program.')
   end
   if others # '' then
      lines<-1> = ''
      lines<-1> = 'no.query makes catalog take an entry of the same name out of the other catalogs without asking: ' : change(others, @fm, ', ') : '.  That is why the name is asked for.'
   end
   gosub gate.line
   typed.name = (if others # '' then pname else '')
   call $tk_confirm(sent, lines, typed.name, res, cmsg)
   if res # 'run' then
      msg = cmsg
      return
   end
   gosub run.sent
   if rerr # '' then
      msg = rerr
      return
   end
   msg = (if said # '' then said else sent : ' ran')
   gosub after.run
   return

* X: take a local entry out and delete the compiled program it points at
do.decat:
   if ns < 1 then return
   mk = shown<ci>
   gosub ensure.meta
   lid = rloc<mk, 1>
   if lid = '' then
      msg = 'there is no local catalog entry for this program: D takes a private one out'
      return
   end
   fn = lid
   gosub check.name
   if not(okname) or index('abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789', lid[1, 1], 1) = 0 or index(kwords, ' ' : downcase(lid) : ' ', 1) > 0 then
      bad.w = lid
      gosub why.bad
      msg = 'this entry name ' : bad.ch : ', which the page does not give to a command: type decatalog ' : lid : ' at the prompt'
      return
   end
   * decatalog deletes the object file the entry points at, and the verb does not ask whether this account may reach that path: an entry that leads outside the account is not offered
   if rtype<mk> # 'p' and (rpath<mk> = '' or not(kernel(K$PATH.OK, rpath<mk>))) then
      msg = lid : ' leads outside this account: the page does not run decatalog on it; type decatalog ' : lid : ' at the prompt'
      return
   end
   sent = 'decatalog ' : lid
   lines = ''
   lines<-1> = 'Takes the local catalog entry ' : lid : ' out of the VOC AND deletes the compiled program it points at: ' : (if rtype<mk> = 'p' then meta<1, 12> else rpath<mk>) : '.'
   lines<-1> = 'The source is not touched; B compiles the program again, but until then it cannot be run.  D would take only the entry out.'
   gosub gate.line
   call $tk_confirm(sent, lines, lid, res, cmsg)
   if res # 'run' then
      msg = cmsg
      return
   end
   gosub run.sent
   if rerr # '' then
      msg = rerr
      return
   end
   msg = (if said # '' then said else sent : ' ran')
   gosub after.run
   return

* D: take a private or a local entry out of the catalogue (the entry only: the compiled program stays)
do.delcat:
   if ns < 1 then return
   mk = shown<ci>
   gosub ensure.meta
   hasp = (meta<1, 5> # '')
   hasl = (rloc<mk, 1> # '')
   if not(hasp) and not(hasl) then
      msg = "there is no private or local catalog entry for this program (a global one is the administrator's to take out: delete.catalog name global)"
      return
   end
   which = 0
   begin case
      case hasp and hasl
         screen msgbox 'Which entry of ' : rname<mk> : '?' : @fm : '' : @fm : 'The private copy, or the local VOC entry.' title 'Take out of the catalog' buttons '&Private,&Local,&Cancel' default 3 returning which else which = 3
      case hasp
         which = 1
      case 1
         which = 2
   end case
   if which # 1 and which # 2 then
      msg = 'nothing removed'
      return
   end
   cname = (if which = 1 then rname<mk> else rloc<mk, 1>)
   fn = cname
   gosub check.name
   if not(okname) or index('abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789', cname[1, 1], 1) = 0 or index(kwords, ' ' : downcase(cname) : ' ', 1) > 0 then
      bad.w = cname
      gosub why.bad
      msg = 'this entry name ' : bad.ch : ', which the page does not give to a command: type delete.catalog ' : cname : (if which = 2 then ' local' else '') : ' at the prompt'
      return
   end
   sent = 'delete.catalog ' : cname : (if which = 2 then ' local' else '')
   lines = ''
   if which = 1 then
      lines<-1> = 'Takes ' : cname : " out of the private catalog (your account's cat file).  The compiled program in its .out file stays; C catalogs it again."
   end else
      lines<-1> = 'Takes the local catalog entry ' : cname : ' (a VOC entry) out.  The compiled program it pointed at stays; X would delete that too.'
   end
   gosub gate.line
   call $tk_confirm(sent, lines, cname, res, cmsg)
   if res # 'run' then
      msg = cmsg
      return
   end
   gosub run.sent
   if rerr # '' then
      msg = rerr
      return
   end
   msg = (if said # '' then said else sent : ' ran')
   gosub after.run
   return

do.filter:
   screen ask 'Part of a program or file name (empty shows every program)' width 40 value ai.arg title 'Filter' returning ft then got = 1 else got = 0
   if not(got) then return
   filt = trim(ft)
   gosub apply.filter
   ci = 1 ; ta = 0
   gosub draw.all
   msg = (if filt = '' then 'every program' else ns : ' with "' : filt : '"')
   return

end

